sitory: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-7\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sketches\" kind=\"sketches\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user synchronizes or imports purchase-order and receiving records from the procurement source. The system records vendor, costs, head counts, weights, breed, age, source, and receiving date against the imported records and establishes the lot's financial and animal-entry baseline.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user maps a PO line to one lot or splits it across multiple lots. The system preserves the PO-line-to-lot traceability and the allocated quantities and weights for each resulting lot.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user associates lots with pens using source pen IDs, capacities, and current animal counts. The system displays the PO → lot → pen relationships and uses lot/pen associations in downstream feeding and performance views.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After receiving data is recorded, the system sets entry weight and receiving-date baselines and calculates each lot's target weight and projected market date from its lifecycle targets and available weight/gain inputs.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If imported records are malformed, required values are missing, or source data cannot be reached, the system reports which records failed and why, and does not silently create incomplete lots.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a repeated synchronization contains already-imported source records, the system avoids duplicating them and reflects changed source values without losing traceability to the original PO and receiving records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If allocations exceed a PO line's received head count or weight, or a pen assignment exceeds its capacity, the system flags the conflict and does not accept the invalid allocation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat procurement PO lines as traceable source records that may map to one or multiple lots; lots and pen assignments retain the source relationships.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user creates or updates a feed inventory item with name, category, quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, and storage location. The system shows current available stock and its opening, received, consumed, and closing quantities.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When stock is received, consumed, or otherwise adjusted, the system records a stock movement and updates the displayed balance and movement history.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user sets a wastage ratio. The system applies it to estimated consumption and shows inventory projections for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user creates or edits a ration by selecting ingredients and entering quantities or proportions, ration type, dry matter, energy, and intended animal type or weight range. The system calculates the recipe's cost per pound from ingredient quantities and unit costs and displays the recipe's nutrition and cost information.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user compares ration mixes using their calculated costs and available nutrition/energy information; the system surfaces the relative cost and nutrition trade-offs to support cost-benefit decisions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system rejects or flags recipes with missing ingredients, invalid or inconsistent proportions, unavailable ingredient references, or ingredient quantities that cannot be priced, and does not present an unreliable calculated cost as valid.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a movement would make available stock negative, the system blocks or flags it and shows the affected item and shortage rather than silently recording an impossible balance.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If there is insufficient consumption history or no configured wastage ratio, the system identifies the affected forecast as unavailable or based on an explicitly displayed default rather than presenting it as a reliable estimate.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat inventory projections as estimates over the requested horizon, with the configured wastage ratio applied to projected consumption; ration comparisons use available recipe, cost, and nutrition data rather than promising biological outcomes.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user generates or enters a dated feeding plan for a pen using its animal count, daily bunk rate, selected ration, and planned delivery time. The system records planned quantity, quantity per animal, selected lot allocation, expected energy intake, estimated feed cost, and plan status.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user updates a plan's status among Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped. The system displays the plan and its status for the selected pen and date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user records a feeding activity against a pen and lot allocation, including date, ration, planned quantity, actual delivered quantity, and status. The system calculates variance as actual quantity minus planned quantity and calculates event feed cost and energy from the ration and actual quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On saving an activity, the system records ingredient consumption according to the ration mix, adjusts inventory, and rolls up feed quantity and cost to the applicable lot. The activity and resulting inventory and lot totals are visible in their histories.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system compares planned and actual feeding and shows the variance, enabling users to identify overfeeding or underfeeding against the plan.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the ration, pen, date, lot allocation, or quantities required for an activity are invalid or missing, the system identifies the problem and does not save a partial activity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the ration ingredients exceed available inventory, the system reports the shortage and does not silently decrement inventory below zero or record inconsistent activity and lot totals.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If saving the feeding event or its inventory and lot updates fails, the system reports failure and leaves the event and related balances consistent, without a duplicate consumption on retry.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"For pens containing multiple lots, feeding plans and activity records are pen-level but identify the lot or lot allocation they apply to; separate allocations can be recorded for multiple lots in the same pen.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user records a lot, measurement date, number of animals weighed, average animal weight, total lot weight, and optional notes. The system stores the reading as a new point in that lot's weight history.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When a prior reading is available, the system calculates and displays weight gain since the previous reading and makes the new 