kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system rejects or reports malformed, incomplete, duplicate, or conflicting import records, identifies affected rows, and does not create duplicate lots or silently overwrite prior mappings; a user can correct and retry rejected records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The procurement and mapping views work as a responsive web app at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treat procurement/receiving imports as source data that can be reconciled into one or more traceable lots per PO line, then assigned to pens; lifecycle targets are calculated from receiving data and configurable target assumptions.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user records feed inventory items with category, quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, and storage location; the system displays current available quantities and item costs.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When stock is received, consumed, adjusted, or wasted, the system records a dated stock movement and updates opening stock, receipts, consumption, wastage, and closing stock; movements that would make available stock negative are blocked or clearly flagged for authorized correction.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user sets or changes a wastage ratio; projected consumption and required procurement quantities reflect that ratio, and the displayed forecast makes the applied rate visible.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system forecasts ingredient balances and potential shortages for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons from available stock and expected demand; unavailable demand inputs are identified rather than presented as 