gy and retains the activity against its pen and lot allocation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"On saving a valid feeding activity, the system deducts each ration ingredient according to the recipe and actual quantity, applies configured wastage where relevant, records ingredient movements, and updates cumulative feed consumption and feed cost for affected lots.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a ration, pen, lot allocation, or inventory balance is missing or invalid, the system explains what must be corrected and does not silently record a completed activity with incorrect stock or cost; authorized users can correct or void an erroneous activity with corresponding movement and rollup adjustments.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can mark a planned feeding in progress, completed, or skipped; skipped feedings do not consume inventory, and the system preserves the reason or status for operational review.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Planning and feeding-entry views are responsive web pages for phone, tablet, and desktop, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"A pen may contain animals from multiple lots; a feeding plan and activity are associated with the pen and can allocate consumption and cost to the relevant lot or lots.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-4\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user records a lot, measurement date, number weighed, average animal weight, and optional notes; the system saves the reading in the lot's dated history and calculates total measured weight and change from the prior reading when possible.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The lot history displays measurements chronologically and exposes entry weight, current weight, and changes over time; adding a later measurement updates the displayed latest reading without deleting earlier readings.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system flags invalid dates, nonpositive weights or counts, and readings that conflict with prior data for review; if no prior reading exists, it records the baseline and does not invent a gain value.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Weight-entry and history views are responsive web pages for phone, tablet, and desktop, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Weight readings are lot-level time-series observations; total lot weight and gain are derived from the recorded average weight and number weighed where those values are available.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-5\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For each lot, the system displays days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total feed consumed, FCR, feed cost per pound of gain, and projected ship date from receiving, feeding, and weight records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After a feeding or weight event is saved or corrected, the system refreshes affected lot totals and derived metrics so dashboards and reports reflect the new data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When dates, entry/current weights, feed totals, or gain are insufficient—or gain is zero or negative—the system marks dependent metrics unavailable or not meaningful instead of showing misleading divisions or projections.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system uses current gain trends and target weights to show projected sale readiness/date and actionable feeding or sale-timing suggestions; it indicates when data is insufficient to make a dependable suggestion.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Users can inspect the source readings and feeding totals behind a lot metric or prediction, so a changed result can be related to the recorded events.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Performance and insight views are responsive web pages for phone, tablet, and desktop, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Use the supplied formulas: FCR is feed consumed divided by weight gained, and feed-to-gain ratio refers to that same efficiency measure; recompute lot metrics when feeding or weight events change.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-6\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The operational dashboard shows active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rates, planned versus actual feed, feed consumed and cost, starting/current weight, gain, ADG, feed-to-gain/FCR, cost of gain, energy consumed, and best/worst performing lots.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user filters dashboards and reports by date range and available lot, pen, breed, or sex attributes; the system updates the displayed rows and aggregates to match the selected filters and indicates when no records match.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Reports answer which pen consumed most, which lots lead in FCR or ADG, which ration is used most, plan-versus-actual alignment, over/underfeeding, remaining inventory, and cost per unit of gain.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user exports the selected feed-to-gain report as CSV or PDF; exported values and filters correspond to the on-screen selection, and export failures are reported without implying a file was created.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The yard summary aggregates active-lot head count, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost across the yard; it identifies unavailable aggregates when 