ngChosen\": \"Treat this as a request for a runnable web-app demo populated with clearly identified synthetic data, plus presentation materials that explain the solution and its readiness—not a request to deploy a native app.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An authorized user imports PO and receiving records containing vendor, costs, head count, weights, breed, age, and source; successfully validated records are saved and linked to their source PO/receiving records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system validates required fields and compatible quantities and weights, reports invalid or incomplete rows, and does not silently create incomplete mappings. Re-imported records are identified so they do not create unintended duplicates.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A user maps a PO line to one or more lots and links lots to pens; the system retains the PO-line-to-lot-to-pen relationships and displays source head counts, weights, costs, pen capacity, and current animal counts for reconciliation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The system flags mappings whose head counts do not reconcile with received quantities or pen capacity, and prevents or clearly identifies invalid assignments rather than silently accepting them.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"For a lot with receiving weight and a target weight, the system records a projected target weight and market/ship date using the configured gain assumption or available lot performance trend; the projection is recalculated when relevant receiving, target, or performance data changes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If required weight, target, receiving date, or gain information is missing or unusable, the system indicates that a lifecycle projection is unavailable instead 